<revisionlist>
  <revision rev="1" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>12013b46cfddc7b06c200dca90683611</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4.5</version>
    <time>1786461185</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package: opentui 0.4.5, the native core of the OpenTUI terminal UI library.

Supersedes SR#1370385, which shipped a libopentui.so built for the OBS
worker's CPU: zig build -Dtarget=native leaves the CPU model at host
detection, so on an aarch64 worker with FEAT_LRCPC (ARMv8.3) yoga's C++
compiled down to ldapr/stlur and the library died with SIGILL on any older
aarch64 - ThunderX2, Cortex-A72 - the moment yoga laid out its first node.
Reproduced with opencode in a Tumbleweed container on an affected machine.

opentui-baseline-cpu.patch pins cpu_model to .baseline. -Dtarget=native is
kept, so the host libc and libstdc++ are still what the library links
against; only the code generator changes. An objdump check at %install fails
the build if the instructions ever reappear after a rebase.

Everything else is unchanged from #1370385. Builds on x86_64 and aarch64,
%check green, rpmlint clean. The same container that crashed now renders and
drives the full TUI.</comment>
    <requestid>1370419</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>ae2e30049984ee68f57605b205bbbdf2</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4.5</version>
    <time>1789573278</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>opentui 0.4.5: the highlighter's grammar modules in opentui-devel become symlinks to the tree-sitter-{javascript,typescript,markdown,zig}-wasm packages' modules (Requires on the devel subpackage) instead of the copies in the source tree. Local build green; the three tests.terminal_test failures seen locally are pre-existing (unmodified r2 fails them here too, OBS passes).
INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (will not build until these land): sr#1378013 tree-sitter, sr#1378025 tree-sitter-javascript, sr#1378034 tree-sitter-typescript, sr#1378029 tree-sitter-markdown, sr#1378039 tree-sitter-zig.</comment>
    <requestid>1378041</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>2d2fa092212e57f7c5170b757aee015e</srcmd5>
    <version>0.5.12</version>
    <time>1790585261</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update opentui to 0.5.12, tracking opencode v2's exact @opentui/* pin across the unversioned FFI ABI. Reworks the packaging for upstream's moved Zig sources (zig 0.16, in-tree vendored deps) and extends the licence tag for the newly bundled wuffs and libwebp code. Test report: local aarch64 build green, rpmlint clean, 2173/2183 Zig tests pass.
</comment>
    <requestid>1380982</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>7c73fd8faf362d358519fb744a874f8a</srcmd5>
    <version>0.5.14</version>
    <time>1791051294</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.5.14, which also carries 0.5.13. Fixes a native text
buffer leak and a missing repaint after net-zero resize bursts, plus
a solid portal listener leak and a Yoga NaN rerender loop. Same
artifact set and Zig pin; unblocks opencode 2.0.22, which requires
opentui = 0.5.14 exactly.</comment>
    <requestid>1382250</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
